From 4cdd4622150019f2764d79142afc462bc7e9ed8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:07:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] Relay-mode Linux guests: carry the platform policy
 carriers from the host config to the supervisor's gate

The relay-mode (legacy) control guest had no way to receive policy carriers: the launcher forwarded none, gsup's legacy
supervisor environment held only the baked flavor and the fw_cfg wallet-policy names, and the shipped host-admission bundle
(40e8ba71) names no fleet mirror. Once the administrator anchors a policy, such a host could never load it and refused itself.

- metal/guest/measured-control.mjs: checkPolicyCarriers is the measured guest's carrier schema, exported and used by both
  modes. A carrier must be ANOTHER host's role: this host's own public origin, the QEMU host link and loopback names are
  refused (its own roles serve only once it is admitted, so a cold start would wait on itself). guestPolicyCarriers and
  withPolicyCarriersEnv give the legacy guest exactly one supervisor name, only from fw_cfg, applied last; an invalid
  setting or a bundle that cannot honour it becomes a value the gate refuses (work and service refused, never admission).
- metal/enclave-metal.mjs: cfg.platformPolicyCarriers is checked and written to fw_cfg in its checked form; invalid or self
  carriers refuse the launch; a direct control guest takes carriers only inside its HOST_DATA-bound config.
- metal/guest/gsup.mjs: the legacy branch checks the fw_cfg setting again and wraps the supervisor environment once, last.
- test/relay-policy-carriers.test.mjs: schema parity with the direct member, refusals, the env boundary, the real launcher
  (fake QEMU), and the supervisor's own gate block on a real local chain: unanchored admits; an anchored policy admits from
  another host's policy mirror with the four former fleet mirrors refused; the admin's ban refuses (sticky) and the next
  anchored document readmits; stale/substituted bytes and invalid settings never admit; the old fec43a6a composition never
  admits under the anchor (negative control). Two existing gsup pins gain the new wrapper.
